//
// Hardware smoke for the fused rn3 conv3x3+conv3x3 pair (Phase H step 2).
//
// Builds one fused-pair ELF (tiny shape, 8×8 tile / ic=mid=ocb=4) and
// runs one xrt.run with a (T+4)×(T+4) input patch + concatenated
// (w1, bn1, w2, bn2) weights. Compares the NPU output against a
// scalar CPU oracle (rn3_pair_pythoc.rn3_pair_fused_bf16 reimplemented
// in numpy, matched bf16 quantization on inputs/weights, kernel's SiLU
// approximation). PASS within rtol=atol=2e-2.
//
// The on-device kernel is intentionally scalar (recomputes conv1 values
// for every conv2 step) — this test anchors the geometry/layout before
// the vectorized implementation lands.
//
// REQUIRES: ryzen_ai_npu2, peano, torch
//
// RUN: rm -rf test_stx
// RUN: mkdir -p test_stx
// RUN: cd test_stx
//
// RUN: env MDV6_BUILD_DIR=. %run_on_npu2% python3 %S/conv/test_rn3_pair_hw.py --layer all
